   "source": [
    "from langchain_ollama import ChatOllama\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "llm = ChatOllama(\n",
    "    model=\"beam:cloud\",\n",
    "    temperature=0.9\n",
    ")\n",
    "response = llm.invoke(\n",
    "    \"Is there any MCP exposed here?\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(response.content)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n"
   ],
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "I don't see any MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers or tools exposed in this session — my available toolset doesn't include any MCP-backed capabilities here.\n",
      "\n",
      "If you're asking about a specific repo, service, or environment you have in mind, could you clarify? For example:\n",
      "\n",
      "- A particular MCP server you expected to be running (e.g., filesystem, GitHub, database, browser)?\n",
      "- A config file (like `claude_desktop_config.json` or a `.mcp.json`) you'd like me to reason about?\n",
      "- Whether an MCP server is exposed on a network endpoint you can share?\n",
      "\n",
      "With more context I can give you a more useful answer (or if you paste config/snippet, help debug why a server isn't being picked up).\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
